➢ 3.1.1 Flagship programs
The literacy activities in this chapter form the foundation of SAL's reading programs and should be implemented regularly throughout the school year. Weekly library activities and bi-monthly book clubs sessions help learners build the skills and confidence they need to participate in larger annual literacy initiatives such as;
These programs provide learners with opportunities to apply their reading, communication, creativity and critical thinking skills in fun, engaging and collaborative ways. They also strengthen learners' confidence, empathy, teamwork and resilience by encouraging them to share ideas, express themselves and learn from one another.

3.3 Life Skills & Values Integration in Reading Activities Teacher-librarians should intentionally connect reading activities to learner’s everyday lives.
During reading activities such as Q&A, role paly, storytelling etc., facilitators should guide learners to reflect on:
❖ decision making;
❖ communication;
❖ teamwork;
❖ problem solving;
❖ leadership;
❖ self-awareness;
❖ empathy and
kindness;
❖ confidence and
self-expression;
❖ respect for
others;
❖ responsibility and
honesty.
Sample life skill reflection Questions
✓ What lesson did you learn from the story?
✓ Was the character decision right or wrong? Why?
✓ What would you do differently?
✓ How did the character show kindness, honesty or courage?
✓ What challenges did the character face and how were they solved?
✓ What can we learn from this story in our daily lives?
✓ How can we apply this lesson at home or at school?
